1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,990
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:04,170
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:04,170 --> 00:00:05,370
don't accept that.

4
00:00:05,570 --> 00:00:06,430
I've been cutting hair

5
00:00:06,430 --> 00:00:08,290
in a barbershop for thirty
years.

6
00:00:08,330 --> 00:00:09,960
On my feet behind the
chair,

7
00:00:09,960 --> 00:00:10,970
all day long.

8
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:11,940
I had my right knee

9
00:00:11,940 --> 00:00:13,440
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:15,660
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:16,230 --> 00:00:18,480
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,900
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:20,930
and it went away.

14
00:00:20,990 --> 00:00:22,330
This is different.

15
00:00:22,370 --> 00:00:23,160
Tight.

16
00:00:23,220 --> 00:00:23,900
Full.

17
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:24,750
Like a band around

18
00:00:24,750 --> 00:00:26,590
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:26,630 --> 00:00:27,790
And for two years I've

20
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:29,270
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:30,290
Give it time.

22
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:32,110
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:32,110 --> 00:00:33,490
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:35,110
At three months,

25
00:00:35,110 --> 00:00:36,070
give it six.

26
00:00:36,180 --> 00:00:37,130
At six months,

27
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:38,880
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:38,920 --> 00:00:39,870
At a year,

29
00:00:39,870 --> 00:00:41,570
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:41,640 --> 00:00:42,870
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:42,910 --> 00:00:44,190
We went down the list.

32
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:45,610
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:45,650 --> 00:00:47,330
Every session,

34
00:00:47,330 --> 00:00:48,850
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:48,940 --> 00:00:50,010
I got stronger.

36
00:00:50,100 --> 00:00:51,530
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:51,570 --> 00:00:52,750
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:52,750 --> 00:00:54,050
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:54,150 --> 00:00:56,120
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:56,120 --> 00:00:57,240
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:57,240 --> 00:00:58,460
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:00:58,590 --> 00:00:59,980
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:00,060 --> 00:01:02,720
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:02,760 --> 00:01:05,660
And after that, a second
operation

45
00:01:05,660 --> 00:01:06,240
to go back

46
00:01:06,240 --> 00:01:07,600
in and do it over.

47
00:01:07,960 --> 00:01:08,990
I said no.

48
00:01:09,080 --> 00:01:11,270
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:12,320
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:12,320 --> 00:01:14,080
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:14,080 --> 00:01:16,620
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:16,710 --> 00:01:18,220
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,220 --> 00:01:19,670
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:19,860 --> 00:01:21,160
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:21,160 --> 00:01:22,260
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:23,950
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:25,330
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's

58
00:01:25,330 --> 00:01:27,620
game without shifting
every two minutes.

59
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:28,620
It woke me at night,

60
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:30,720
and it turned ordinary
things,

61
00:01:30,720 --> 00:01:31,670
like getting in the car

62
00:01:31,670 --> 00:01:32,990
or up off the couch,

63
00:01:32,990 --> 00:01:34,280
into a decision.

64
00:01:34,480 --> 00:01:35,770
Halfway through a fade,

65
00:01:35,770 --> 00:01:36,550
I'd have to stop

66
00:01:36,550 --> 00:01:37,870
and lean on the chair.

67
00:01:38,470 --> 00:01:40,080
And my regulars noticed.

68
00:01:40,180 --> 00:01:41,310
After a long and serious

69
00:01:41,310 --> 00:01:42,700
talk with my husband,

70
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,530
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,110
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:47,760
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:47,850 --> 00:01:49,230
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:49,230 --> 00:01:51,840
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:51,880 --> 00:01:53,900
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:53,900 --> 00:01:54,920
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:56,130
Only this time there

78
00:01:56,130 --> 00:01:57,400
was no new number.

79
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,990
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:00,030 --> 00:02:01,740
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:02,810
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:02,810 --> 00:02:03,910
lot for a while.

83
00:02:03,970 --> 00:02:05,400
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:05,440 --> 00:02:06,710
Then explain this.

85
00:02:06,830 --> 00:02:09,060
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,500
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:12,630
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:12,770 --> 00:02:14,740
I had my first customer at
eight.

89
00:02:14,870 --> 00:02:16,630
Everyone in the house was
asleep

90
00:02:16,630 --> 00:02:18,180
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

91
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,180
with my leg up,

92
00:02:19,180 --> 00:02:20,560
trying to find any angle
where

93
00:02:20,560 --> 00:02:22,070
it didn't feel like
something was wrapped

94
00:02:22,070 --> 00:02:23,660
around my knee and
tightening.

95
00:02:23,910 --> 00:02:26,240
My husband didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

96
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:28,360
By then I'd stopped
telling him.

97
00:02:28,970 --> 00:02:30,130
And I just thought,

98
00:02:30,130 --> 00:02:31,900
is this really my life
now?

99
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,020
How many more years could

100
00:02:33,020 --> 00:02:34,720
I stand behind that chair?

101
00:02:34,790 --> 00:02:36,260
I can't live like this.

102
00:02:36,350 --> 00:02:38,550
So I made myself a
promise.

103
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:39,740
I wouldn't go a day

104
00:02:39,740 --> 00:02:41,360
without looking for an
answer.

105
00:02:41,490 --> 00:02:42,840
And when I found one,

106
00:02:42,840 --> 00:02:44,030
I'd share it with everyone

107
00:02:44,030 --> 00:02:45,680
going through the same
thing.

108
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:47,580
So I got my laptop

109
00:02:47,580 --> 00:02:48,880
out and went looking.

110
00:02:49,190 --> 00:02:50,580
Not for a product.

111
00:02:50,680 --> 00:02:52,220
For an explanation.

112
00:02:52,260 --> 00:02:53,990
Mayo Clinic forums,

113
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:56,120
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

114
00:02:56,120 --> 00:02:58,720
doctor videos, medical
animations.

115
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:00,560
And that's when I found a
video

116
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:02,510
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

117
00:03:02,550 --> 00:03:04,150
Steven Salinger,

118
00:03:04,150 --> 00:03:05,350
whose own wife had been

119
00:03:05,350 --> 00:03:06,880
through exactly this.

120
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:08,410
But before I say anything
else,

121
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:09,890
I want to be straight with
you.

122
00:03:10,940 --> 00:03:12,950
You've already had
something work fast.

123
00:03:12,990 --> 00:03:13,840
The ice.

124
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:15,780
The first week of a new
pill.

125
00:03:15,820 --> 00:03:17,500
The good day after a
session.

126
00:03:17,650 --> 00:03:19,250
Then it wore off.

127
00:03:19,570 --> 00:03:21,600
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

128
00:03:21,750 --> 00:03:22,960
Fast relief

129
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:24,060
isn't relief.

130
00:03:24,920 --> 00:03:26,040
It's a preview.

131
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:27,270
So I'm not going to tell

132
00:03:27,270 --> 00:03:28,580
you this works fast.

133
00:03:28,620 --> 00:03:29,550
It doesn't.

134
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,430
But if you're willing to
be patient,

135
00:03:31,430 --> 00:03:32,260
and to look at what's

136
00:03:32,260 --> 00:03:33,780
going on around your new
knee

137
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:35,420
instead of inside it,
there

138
00:03:35,420 --> 00:03:37,510
is a real reason it still
hurts.

139
00:03:37,550 --> 00:03:39,620
And something you can do
about it.

140
00:03:39,760 --> 00:03:41,490
Let me explain what he
said,

141
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:43,090
because this is what
changed

142
00:03:43,090 --> 00:03:44,330
everything for me.

143
00:03:44,370 --> 00:03:46,080
He started with the
basics.

144
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:47,830
A knee replacement takes
out

145
00:03:47,830 --> 00:03:49,470
the worn joint surfaces

146
00:03:49,470 --> 00:03:51,410
and puts in metal and
plastic.

147
00:03:51,500 --> 00:03:53,190
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

148
00:03:53,190 --> 00:03:54,930
you had before the
operation.

149
00:03:55,210 --> 00:03:56,780
That part I already knew.

150
00:03:56,830 --> 00:03:58,190
But then he explained
something

151
00:03:58,190 --> 00:03:59,750
nobody had ever told me.

152
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,150
He said,

153
00:04:01,150 --> 00:04:02,420
think about a swollen foot

154
00:04:02,420 --> 00:04:03,600
inside a shoe.

155
00:04:03,720 --> 00:04:05,050
The shoe didn't shrink.

156
00:04:05,180 --> 00:04:07,200
Your foot is taking up
more room,

157
00:04:07,200 --> 00:04:08,560
so everything feels
cramped

158
00:04:08,560 --> 00:04:10,070
and tight and squeezed.

159
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:11,220
Your new knee sits

160
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:12,430
in a limited space

161
00:04:12,430 --> 00:04:14,690
with living tissue packed
all around it.

162
00:04:14,850 --> 00:04:16,630
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

163
00:04:16,630 --> 00:04:18,300
had to work through that
tissue.

164
00:04:18,450 --> 00:04:21,170
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

165
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:22,870
At first that's normal.

166
00:04:22,980 --> 00:04:24,030
But in some people

167
00:04:24,030 --> 00:04:25,470
that swelling can stay
switched

168
00:04:25,470 --> 00:04:27,400
on far longer than
expected.

169
00:04:27,470 --> 00:04:29,230
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:29,230 --> 00:04:30,900
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:30,950 --> 00:04:32,340
So when you bend,

172
00:04:32,340 --> 00:04:33,990
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:35,220
When you straighten,

174
00:04:35,220 --> 00:04:36,570
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:37,720
That's the band.

176
00:04:37,810 --> 00:04:40,000
That's the ache that never
quite leaves.

177
00:04:40,490 --> 00:04:41,270
And you start being

178
00:04:41,270 --> 00:04:42,280
the one who says,

179
00:04:42,280 --> 00:04:43,360
you go ahead.

180
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:44,600
I'll stay here.

181
00:04:44,670 --> 00:04:46,160
And that's exactly why so
much

182
00:04:46,160 --> 00:04:47,800
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

183
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,960
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

184
00:04:49,960 --> 00:04:50,890
around the knee.

185
00:04:50,970 --> 00:04:51,930
Worth doing,

186
00:04:51,930 --> 00:04:52,860
and I'd done it.

187
00:04:52,970 --> 00:04:54,280
It does nothing about
tissue

188
00:04:54,280 --> 00:04:55,410
taking up room.

189
00:04:55,470 --> 00:04:56,590
A nerve block quiets

190
00:04:56,590 --> 00:04:58,240
the nerve carrying the
signal.

191
00:04:58,410 --> 00:05:00,570
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

192
00:05:01,100 --> 00:05:02,650
But when that irritated
tissue

193
00:05:02,650 --> 00:05:04,250
finally calms down,

194
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:05,680
it holds less fluid,

195
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:07,320
and it takes up less room.

196
00:05:07,430 --> 00:05:08,740
Less room taken up means

197
00:05:08,740 --> 00:05:10,710
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

198
00:05:10,750 --> 00:05:12,530
That's what takes the
pressure off.

199
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,210
After two years of this,

200
00:05:14,210 --> 00:05:15,730
it finally made sense.

201
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:18,240
The problem was never the
new knee.

202
00:05:18,340 --> 00:05:20,230
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

203
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:21,810
He calls it the squeeze.

204
00:05:21,850 --> 00:05:24,030
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

205
00:05:24,110 --> 00:05:25,370
I'd bought knee sleeves,

206
00:05:25,370 --> 00:05:26,740
compression braces,

207
00:05:26,740 --> 00:05:29,650
a cushioned mat for behind
the chair,

208
00:05:29,650 --> 00:05:32,310
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:32,310 --> 00:05:33,390
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:33,390 --> 00:05:34,510
me was an hour.

211
00:05:34,740 --> 00:05:35,680
I even looked at going

212
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:37,490
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:37,670 --> 00:05:39,180
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:39,180 --> 00:05:41,130
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:41,130 --> 00:05:42,390
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:43,130 --> 00:05:44,290
Then one night

217
00:05:44,290 --> 00:05:45,920
I went back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:47,860
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:49,350
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:49,350 --> 00:05:51,120
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:53,570
comparing notes on
stiffness and tightness

222
00:05:53,570 --> 00:05:55,040
nobody could explain.

223
00:05:55,790 --> 00:05:57,640
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:57,640 --> 00:05:59,450
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:00,870
This one device,

226
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:02,130
and people saying

227
00:06:02,130 --> 00:06:03,190
it was the first thing

228
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:04,400
that made a difference.

229
00:06:04,540 --> 00:06:06,610
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

230
00:06:06,610 --> 00:06:07,980
alright, here it comes,

231
00:06:07,980 --> 00:06:09,400
she's selling me
something,

232
00:06:09,400 --> 00:06:11,060
let me shut that down
right now.

233
00:06:11,220 --> 00:06:13,020
I'm only here because I
made myself

234
00:06:13,020 --> 00:06:15,200
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

235
00:06:15,200 --> 00:06:16,240
that if I ever found

236
00:06:16,240 --> 00:06:17,530
something that helped,

237
00:06:17,530 --> 00:06:18,660
I'd say so.

238
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,460
It's called

239
00:06:20,460 --> 00:06:22,990
the KenRelief Red Light
Therapy Wrap.

240
00:06:23,160 --> 00:06:24,450
At first glance

241
00:06:24,450 --> 00:06:25,630
I didn't buy it.

242
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:26,620
It looked like the cheap

243
00:06:26,620 --> 00:06:28,240
knee sleeves off Amazon

244
00:06:28,240 --> 00:06:29,570
that did nothing for me.

245
00:06:29,790 --> 00:06:31,630
But I went to their
website anyway,

246
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:32,490
just to see what all

247
00:06:32,490 --> 00:06:33,750
the fuss was about.

248
00:06:33,790 --> 00:06:35,900
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

249
00:06:35,900 --> 00:06:38,500
charge $200 a session for,

250
00:06:38,500 --> 00:06:41,240
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

251
00:06:41,240 --> 00:06:42,120
in a wrap you plug

252
00:06:42,120 --> 00:06:43,400
into the wall at home.

253
00:06:43,470 --> 00:06:45,180
Two hundred and forty
lights.

254
00:06:45,300 --> 00:06:47,270
Red at 660 nanometers

255
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:49,710
and near-infrared at 850,

256
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:51,840
run together for the
strongest effect.

257
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:53,510
Four strength levels.

258
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:55,330
A five to thirty minute
timer.

259
00:06:55,390 --> 00:06:57,010
Then I saw the guarantee.

260
00:06:57,070 --> 00:06:58,170
Ninety days.

261
00:06:58,230 --> 00:07:00,060
Results or your money
back,

262
00:07:00,060 --> 00:07:02,370
no questions, no store
credit,

263
00:07:02,370 --> 00:07:04,000
and you don't even send it
back.

264
00:07:04,530 --> 00:07:06,710
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

265
00:07:06,710 --> 00:07:08,220
days to change my mind.

266
00:07:08,560 --> 00:07:09,900
There wasn't much to lose,

267
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,050
so I ordered it.

268
00:07:11,400 --> 00:07:12,720
Two of them, actually.

269
00:07:12,880 --> 00:07:15,460
Only the right knee was
replaced,

270
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:17,370
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

271
00:07:17,370 --> 00:07:19,070
and I'd done it for two
years.

272
00:07:19,470 --> 00:07:21,580
The left one was carrying
the difference.

273
00:07:21,800 --> 00:07:22,660
When it came,

274
00:07:22,660 --> 00:07:24,650
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

275
00:07:24,650 --> 00:07:25,690
because I'd been let down

276
00:07:25,690 --> 00:07:27,610
too many times to get
excited.

277
00:07:27,730 --> 00:07:29,050
What I felt was warmth.

278
00:07:29,090 --> 00:07:30,910
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

279
00:07:31,190 --> 00:07:32,770
More like it was coming
from inside

280
00:07:32,770 --> 00:07:34,720
the knee and spreading
around it.

281
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,750
And that was it.

282
00:07:35,790 --> 00:07:37,370
That was the whole
